# Suite nomenclature

- **Authority:** `docs/SUITE.md` (canonical in the MynaHub repository `MynaHub`; keep identical copies in MynaOps, MynaCAD, and update all when terms change).
- **User-visible app names (2026-11-10):** the family is **Myna** (the suite's name; there is no app called Myna: the launcher was removed on 2026-11-11). Apps: **MynaHub** (hub), **MynaCAD** (drafting), **MynaOps** (operations: quantities, estimates, billing), **Myna3D** (3D / BIM, planned). Spell exactly, one word, capital letters as shown. Do not use the retired bird names Kivo, Tren, Falcon or Finch, nor the old names O-Studio, O-CoreOp, O-Draft or O-Form, in menus, dialogs or user-facing sentences. Identifiers (install folders, exe names, `OSTUDIO_*`, ticket ids, the stored origin stamp) keep the old spellings.
- **Suite hub:** **MynaHub** (company file, sign-in, users, roles; opens the sibling apps by path). There is no launcher. Do not refer to **OSAS**, **OSAS.exe**, Myna as an app, or a launcher in user text.
- **Files:** company file = `.osas`; project file = `.osp`. **Take-off** is hyphenated in user text.
- **Assistant:** say **the AI agent** (model **Olmo 3 7B**) on loopback `:8742`. **MynaOps** hosts it (its window, or headless `O-CoreOp.exe --ai-host` that MynaCAD starts); **MynaCAD** is a client; **MynaHub has no AI**.
- **Not in user text:** AQC, AOS, AAD, AADT, ShilpiDB, Tulu, OSAS as a product name, OSAS.exe, and the old app names O-Studio, O-CoreOp, O-Draft, O-Form. Wire constants stay: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\O-Studio\`, `OSTUDIO_*` env vars, ticket ids `O-Studio` / `O-CoreOp` / `O-Draft` / `O-Form`, install folders and executable names, format ids `osp` and `studio-active-project` — see `docs/SUITE.md` and `Office.Shared.SuiteWire`.
- **O-UI:** shared WinUI library in repo **`o-ui`**, assembly **`O.Ui`** (`Hcw.Ui` / hcw-ui retired). Not a user-visible app name.
